invariant: INV-25
file: handshake_parser.c
catches: handshake_strict_test
builds: bin/handshake_strict_test
reason: hsp_parse_certificate accepts a certificate_list shorter than the
  Certificate message, so bytes after the vector are never read and two
  messages carry one chain. RFC 9846 §4.5.1 ends the message at the
  vector. test/handshake_strict_test.c's Certificate pair objects, and so
  does lint-exact-fill, because the equality is the only one on r.

--- old
    if (r.err || len != rb_left(&r) || len == 0) {
--- new
    if (r.err || len > rb_left(&r) || len == 0) {
